[2026-03-29 00:03:20] Audited Chapter 3 Cortex-M4 peripherals and fixed MPU permission mismatch
- Request: Before moving to Chapter 7, use the newly added Documents/cortex-m4.pdf together with the TM4C1294 manual to verify that all Chapter 3 Cortex-M4 sub-peripherals are implemented, identify missing parts, and fix any mismatches found.
- Manual basis: Confirmed from Documents/tm4c1294ncpdt.pdf Chapter 3 table of contents and extracted Chapter 3 text that the scope is SysTick, NVIC, SCB, MPU, and FPU. Confirmed from Documents/cortex-m4.pdf that the generic ARM guide covers the same core-peripheral family under its Chapter 4 even though its Chapter 3 is the instruction set.
- Coverage check: Verified that TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/Core contains SYSTICK, NVIC, SCB, MPU, and FPU modules, and that their register-address and peripheral-struct headers cover the Chapter 3 register map regions documented in the TM4C1294 manual.
- Findings: No Chapter 3 sub-peripheral is missing from the repo. The concrete mismatch found in existing code was in TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/Core/MPU/Driver/xSource/MPU_Init.c, where the overlapping flash-constant MPU region was documented and named as a read-only non-executable flash region but was configured with read/write access permissions.
- Implementation: Updated MPU_Init.c so the flash-constant region uses MPU_RASR_R_AP_RORO instead of MPU_RASR_R_AP_RWRW, and replaced several stale size/address comments with explicit region constants that match the actual programmed MPU region sizes.
- Validation: VS Code diagnostics report no errors in TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/Core/MPU/Driver/xSource/MPU_Init.c after the change.
- Remaining note: MPU__vInit is still marked application-specific inside the raw driver layer and there is no xApplication_MCU/Core/MPU wrapper yet. This is an architectural cleanup item, not a missing Chapter 3 peripheral.